% conduct - soak it, then shock it
%
% The recipe: ?e carries wet (it stands in water, is doused, or is pushed
% into a pool), then someone else lands shocked on it. What wet + shocked
% does is the level's physics (a reaction); the recipe only names the two
% halves of the combo - ab_acts' combo/3 states the roles and confirms the
% simulated world at the end.

% === Methods ===

conduct(?e) :- if(), do(combo(wet, shocked, ?e)).
